{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791586582,"nonce":"2OI07NlxCVOpcAvimw+agEwennQ=","title":"M6: Harden local llama-server setup (API key, CORS) and detect CPU-only builds","message":"1) llama-server warned: no API key set and CORS allows all origins. Bound to 127.0.0.1, but any web page in the user's browser can still call localhost:8080 cross-origin and read responses; /slots can expose cached prompts containing the resume. setup-local-llm.sh should generate a random key (stored in the OS keyring or ~/.env as LLAMA_API_KEY), pass --api-key, and the local scorer should send it as a Bearer token; also disable /slots (--no-slots) and avoid permissive CORS where the build allows. 2) The script recommended GPU placement from nvidia-smi alone, but the Homebrew build is CPU-only (llama-server --list-devices shows only OpenBLAS). Detect backends via --list-devices and adjust the plan and --n-gpu-layers.","files":null}]}